---
import LastseenLayout from '../../layouts/LastseenLayout.astro';
---

<LastseenLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Lastseen"
  description="How the Lastseen app handles data: Bluetooth history and places stay on your phone, crash reports without personal data, no account, no tracking."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-6 pt-10 pb-24 max-w-4xl text-slate-800">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-slate-500 font-medium">Last updated: 2026-11-01</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how the Android app Lastseen, listed on Google Play as “Bluetooth: Last known
        Location” (package <code>com.cmart.bluetoothfinder</code>, “Lastseen”, “we”, “us”), handles data. Lastseen
        records when and where your phone was connected to your Bluetooth devices, so you can find a lost device. In
        short: your history and your locations never leave your phone. Lastseen has no account and no own server. The
        only data we receive are anonymous usage statistics (how many installations use the app) and crash reports,
        both without personal data. You can switch crash reports off.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">1. Controller / Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Controller: Christoph Martin<br />
        Address: Fischerweg 8, 7503 Großpetersdorf, Austria<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">info@endure-cycling.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">2. Data stored on your phone</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Devices: the name and Bluetooth address of devices your phone connects to, and the names you give them</li>
        <li>Events: when a device connected, disconnected, came into range or left range</li>
        <li>
          Places: the position of your phone at these moments, with accuracy and age. Places are only recorded if you
          allow location access.
        </li>
        <li>Gaps: periods in which Lastseen could not record reliably</li>
        <li>Your settings, the start date of your 10-day trial, and whether you own the Lifetime Unlock</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These data are kept in the app's private storage on your phone. They are not sent to us or to anyone else.
        Android's app backup is switched off for Lastseen, so they are not part of your Google device backup either.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">3. Location, also in the background</h2>
      <p>
        Lastseen uses your phone's location to remember where a Bluetooth device was connected or disconnected. A
        device usually gets lost while the app is closed, so Lastseen asks for location access “all the time”. With this
        permission it takes one location fix when a device connects or disconnects, also when the app is closed or not
        in use. During this fix (at most 30 seconds) a notification is shown. Lastseen does not track your location
        continuously and does not record a route.
      </p>
      <p>
        Location data are used only to show you where your devices were. They are stored on your phone only and are
        never transmitted, sold or shared. You can withdraw location access at any time in Android's settings; Lastseen
        then records events without a place.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">4. Bluetooth and nearby devices</h2>
      <p>
        Lastseen uses the Bluetooth permission to see which paired devices connect and disconnect, and Android's
        companion device feature to notice when a linked device comes into or leaves range. Nearby Search scans for
        Bluetooth signals only while you have it open, to show how close a lost device is. Signals of other people's
        devices are not stored.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">5. Map</h2>
      <p>
        When you open a map, Lastseen loads map images for the visible area from OpenFreeMap (tiles.openfreemap.org).
        Like any server, OpenFreeMap sees your IP address and which map area is requested. It does not receive your
        history, your device list or the places Lastseen stored.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">6. Crash and error reports (Sentry)</h2>
      <p>
        When Lastseen crashes, freezes (ANR) or hits an error, it sends a report to Sentry (Functional Software, Inc.,
        USA) so we can fix the problem. A report contains:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Stack trace and error message</li>
        <li>App version, Android version, device maker and model</li>
        <li>A random installation ID and session health (whether a session ended in a crash)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Reports never contain places or coordinates, Bluetooth device names or addresses, screenshots, your name, email
        address or any other personal data; Lastseen removes such fields before sending. Like any server, Sentry sees
        the IP address of the connection that delivers a report. Crash reports are on by default; you can switch them
        off in Settings. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in a working app (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)). Reports are kept
        for up to 90 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        Usage statistics are always on and not affected by this switch: when the app starts and stops, Lastseen sends a
        session ping to Sentry with the random installation ID, app version, Android version and whether the session
        ended in a crash. It tells us how many installations use the app and how stable it is. It contains no places,
        device names, Bluetooth addresses or other personal data. Legal basis and retention as above.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">7. Trial and purchases (Google Play)</h2>
      <p>
        The Lifetime Unlock is sold through Google Play Billing. Google processes the payment as an independent
        controller under its own privacy policy. Lastseen only receives from Google Play whether you own the product and
        the purchase confirmation needed to unlock it. We do not receive your name, email address or payment details.
      </p>
      <p>
        The trial start date is also saved in Google Play services Block Store, so that a reinstall does not restart the
        trial. Block Store keeps this single date with your Google account's device backup, end-to-end encrypted where
        your device supports it. It contains no other data, and we cannot read it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">8. Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        If you allow notifications, Lastseen shows a short notification while it records a place, tells you about a
        newly connected device, warns you when recording is not reliable, and reminds you before your trial ends. All notifications are created on the phone;
        no push service or server is involved.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">9. Exports</h2>
      <p>
        An export of your history or the diagnostic log only leaves your phone if you share it yourself, to a recipient
        you choose.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">10. What we do not do</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>No account, no login, no own server, no cloud sync</li>
        <li>No analytics, no advertising, no tracking SDKs</li>
        <li>No sale or sharing of data with third parties for their own purposes</li>
        <li>No collection of contacts, photos, messages or other personal content</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">11. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Sentry may process crash reports in the United States. Where required, we rely on the EU Standard Contractual
        Clauses and Sentry's data processing agreement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">12. Your rights (EEA/UK/Switzerland)</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability, and the right
        to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (in Austria: Datenschutzbehörde, dsb.gv.at). Because crash
        reports carry no personal identifiers, we usually cannot link a report to you; tell us your device model and the
        approximate time of a crash and we will search for it. Contact:
        <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">info@endure-cycling.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Deleting data: Settings › Data › “Delete history” removes all recorded events and places. Uninstalling Lastseen
        or clearing its storage removes everything stored on the phone. To also remove the trial date from Block Store,
        clear Lastseen's data in the Android settings before uninstalling. Crash reports expire automatically after 90
        days, or earlier on request.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">13. This website</h2>
      <p>
        The Lastseen pages on endure-cycling.com set no cookies and load no analytics. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages
        (GitHub, Inc., USA), which processes your IP address to deliver the pages.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">14. Children</h2>
      <p>Lastseen is not directed at children under 13.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">15. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy. The “Last updated” date above shows the current version.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</LastseenLayout>
